    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Floods happen when too much water covers the land. They can come from heavy rains, rivers that rise too high, or big waves from the sea. Floods can be very dangerous. Every year, thousands of people lose their lives because of floods."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Floods also cause many other serious problems. In 2024, more than 19 million people had to leave their homes because of floods. That’s like moving everyone in a whole country, such as "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Somalia",
            "zh": "索马里"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " or the Netherlands. Floods can also damage roads, bridges, and schools. In 2023, floods in "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Slovenia",
            "zh": "斯洛文尼亚"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " caused damage "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "equal",
            "ref": "v-equal"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to about 16% of the country’s economy. In the United States, floods cost billions of dollars every year. After a flood, food can become hard to find, and dirty water can spread disease."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Floods are becoming more common, and one major reason is rising global temperatures. When the Earth gets warmer, the air can hold more water. This makes rain heavier and storms stronger. Also, dry ground cannot soak up water well. Water flows quickly into low areas, causing flooding."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Another major reason is rising sea levels, which make "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "coastal",
            "zh": "沿海的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " floods worse. Big waves push more water onto the land. Scientists say that by 2100, large floods that used to occur only once every 100 years may occur every year. Many cities may face danger by then."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "So, what can we do? Early warning systems can alert people when floods are "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "approaching",
            "ref": "v-approach"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", giving them time to reach safe places. Building sea walls can help stop floodwater. Cities are also turning into “"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "sponge cities",
            "zh": "海绵城市"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "” by building special streets and green spaces. These features help soak up rainwater, slow it down, and reduce the risk of flooding. But in some places, scientists say the safest solution may be a plan called “"
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "managed retreat"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "”. This means moving people away from areas that flood repeatedly."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Floods are a big challenge. But if we work together and plan well, we can stay safe and protect our homes. By understanding the causes and taking action, we can make a real difference."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
